# Phase 21B condition 1's raw OQMD coverage snapshot (~2.3MB) -- not
# comparable in size to the kononova_sample.jsonl ~500KB precedent
# (docs/thermodynamic_selectivity_calibration.md §6.4/§6.5), so only
# the derived oqmd_coverage_manifest.json (~240KB) and
# oqmd_coverage_gate_result.json ship. Raw entries are reproducible
# from OQMD's own public API.
/benchmarks/data/oqmd_coverage_snapshot.json
# Phase 28 exploration-benchmark intermediate artifacts: both large
# (3.6MB, 11.5MB) and fully deterministic/regenerable from the two
# already-committed source datasets (kononova_sample.jsonl,
# thermodynamic_selectivity_clean_population.json) via
# benchmarks/exploration_build_recall_manifest.py and
# benchmarks/exploration_build_frozen_decoy_catalog.py -- not comparable
# in size to the kononova_sample.jsonl ~500KB commit precedent, matching
# the same rule already applied to oqmd_coverage_snapshot.json.
# exploration_baseline_v0_6_0.json (the actual immutable gate artifact,
# ~285KB) IS committed -- small enough, and the one file this whole
# gate depends on, so a directly git-tracked/auditable history beats a
# regenerable-plus-checksum indirection here.
/benchmarks/data/exploration_recall_manifest.json
/benchmarks/data/exploration_frozen_catalog_manifest.json
# Phase 21B calibration intermediates: both fully regenerable in seconds
# from already-committed source data (oqmd_coverage_gate_result.json,
# thermodynamic_selectivity_clean_population.json, oqmd_coverage_manifest.json)
# via benchmarks/build_phase21b_calibration_input.py then
# examples/exploration_phase21b_calibration.rs -- not comparable in size
# to the kononova_sample.jsonl ~500KB commit precedent (1.0MB, 377KB).
# Only the final analysis (phase21b_calibration_result.json, ~46KB,
# comparable to prior committed exploration-result files) ships.
/benchmarks/data/phase21b_calibration_input.json
/benchmarks/data/exploration_phase21b_calibration_result.json
